layground/docker-beets/compare/nightly-e170aeee-ls8...nightly-5fbf0c03-ls9","upstream":"Fix lastgenre output during import (#7107)\n\n## Description\n\nFixes #6830.\n\nDuring an import, the `lastgenre` plugin prints the fetched genres to\nthe terminal. This output can appear on top of the importer's prompt for\nthe next album, making the import look frozen.\n\nThis PR fixes the issue by preventing the `imported` hook from printing\ngenre changes during an import. The genres are still fetched and saved,\nand `beet lastgenre` continues to display changes as before.\n\nI investigated the code to identify the likely cause. I added a\nregression test to verify that the import stage does not print anything\nand that the genres are still assigned correctly. I also tested the\nchange on Windows and confirmed that the new test fails with the\noriginal code and passes with the fix.\n\nIf someone can reproduce the original issue, I would appreciate\nconfirmation that this fix resolves it.\n\n### AI usage\n\nI used Claude to help me with this contribution. I ran the tests and\nlinter myself .","upstream_url":"https://github.com/beetbox/beets/commit/5fbf0c03ebe2b61a27409b36f6823763f9edaf96"},"config":{"env":["PATH=/lsiopy/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin","PS1=$(whoami)@$(hostname):$(pwd)\\$ ","HOME=/config","TERM=xterm","S6_CMD_WAIT_FOR_SERVICES_MAXTIME=0","S6_VERBOSITY=1","S6_STAGE2_HOOK=/docker-mods","VIRTUAL_ENV=/lsiopy","LSIO_FIRST_PARTY=true","BEETSDIR=/config","EDITOR=nano"],"exposed_ports":["8337/tcp"],"volumes":["/config"],"entrypoint":["/init"],"working_dir":"/"},"is_newest":false,"links":{"build":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-5fbf0c03-ls9.json","diff":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-5fbf0c03-ls9/diff.json","layers":{"amd64":"https://linuxserver-playground.github.io/hub/api/v1/catalog/beets/builds/nightly-5fbf0c03-ls9/layers.amd64.json",